<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Vault Lint LaunchAgent

  Weekly content-hygiene sweep over the vault: duplicate and malformed tags,
  taxonomy drift against Knowledge/Tag Taxonomy.md, near-duplicate notes,
  frontmatter schema gaps, broken wikilinks, and divergence between the
  vault's Templates/Scripts and the public template repo.

  Read-only by design. The scheduled run passes no fixing flags at all: it
  reports, and you decide what to act on. Run the fixers by hand after reading
  the report.

  Mondays at 07:00, after the weekday 05:00 meeting pull and the 06:00 morning
  dashboard, so the week's first dashboard isn't competing with it and the
  report is waiting when the week starts.

  On the exit-zero flag: without it the lint exits 1 whenever it finds
  anything, and morning_dashboard.py reads launchd's LastExitStatus, so a vault
  with two stray tags would render as a failed pipeline. Exit status here means
  "the lint ran"; the findings live in the log.

  No verbose flag on purpose: the full listing runs to hundreds of lines of
  unreferenced People notes and buries the findings that need action. The log
  keeps counts and samples; run it by hand with verbose to see everything.

  NOTE for editors: XML comments cannot contain a double hyphen, so flag names
  are written here without their leading dashes. Adding them makes this file
  unparseable by plistlib even though plutil and launchd still accept it, and
  the dashboard would quietly drop this job from pipeline health.

  Stdlib-only, using /usr/bin/python3 so the sweep runs even if the per-vault
  venv is broken (the same reason the security jobs do).
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>Label</key>
    <string>com.obsidian.vault-lint</string>

    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
        <string>/usr/bin/python3</string>
        <string>/Users/YOUR_USERNAME/Obsidian/Templates/Scripts/vault_lint.py</string>
        <string>--exit-zero</string>
    </array>

    <key>StartCalendarInterval</key>
    <dict>
        <key>Weekday</key><integer>1</integer>
        <key>Hour</key><integer>7</integer>
        <key>Minute</key><integer>0</integer>
    </dict>

    <key>RunAtLoad</key>
    <false/>

    <key>StandardOutPath</key>
    <string>/Users/YOUR_USERNAME/Library/Logs/vault-lint.log</string>
    <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
    <string>/Users/YOUR_USERNAME/Library/Logs/vault-lint.log</string>
</dict>
</plist>
